  "description": "Works to trees protected by a preservation order. Oak T1 - (8/93 - T10) -&nbsp; Crown Lift to 3m. Reduce back from building to give 2m clearance . Remove deadwood. Reduce overextended limbs back in line with canopy by 2m from branch ends. Carry out an aerial inspection.&nbsp;Oak\r\nT2 - (8/93 - T9) – Prune back secondary growth from lowest westerly limb\r\noverhanging building, by shortening back lower branches by approximately 2m, to\r\nsuitable growth points. Reduce upper canopy back from building by 2-3m. Lift\r\ncanopy over pavement to 3m and Highway to 4.5m, and balance remainder in\r\nproportion to the tree's original shape. Remove deadwood, including dead\r\nhanging ivy.&nbsp;(Amended Description).\r\n\r\n&nbsp;",
